47
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:27,616
How does logs in depth work?

48
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:37,360
Docker captures everything a container's main process writes to standard output (stdout) and standard error (stderr),

49
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:43,174
and stores it through a logging driver (by default json-file, lesson 102).

50
00:03:43,174 --> 00:03:45,217
docker logs reads it back.

51
